{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","id":"7c3403fd7f9e258b098078db","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp%40gmail.com/","channels":["dmaengine"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:08:54.557Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp@gmail.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCHv2] dmaengine: at_hdmac: fix sparse '__iomem' cast warning in memset helpers","messages":{"an-EvmZ2BtoKW8kX@lizhi-Precision-Tower-5810":{"id":"an-EvmZ2BtoKW8kX@lizhi-Precision-Tower-5810","messageId":"an-EvmZ2BtoKW8kX@lizhi-Precision-Tower-5810","references":["20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260724225958.43925-1-rosenp@gmail.com"],"author":{"name":"Frank Li","address":"Frank.li@oss.nxp.com"},"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T21:12:30.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T21:12:30.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCHv2] dmaengine: at_hdmac: fix sparse '__iomem' cast warning in memset helpers","mailingLists":[{"id":"dmaengine.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"dmaengine.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Fri, Jul 24, 2026 at 03:59:58PM -0700, Rosen Penev wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Both atc_prep_dma_memset() and atc_prep_dma_memset_sg() declare vaddr"},{"depth":1,"text":"as 'void __iomem *' but assign the return of dma_pool_alloc(), which"},{"depth":1,"text":"returns 'void *' (not iomem memory). This causes sparse to warn about"},{"depth":1,"text":"a cast removing the __iomem address space at the dereference site."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The struct field memset_vaddr is also typed as 'int *', which is"},{"depth":1,"text":"neither the type returned by dma_pool_alloc() nor the type used for"},{"depth":1,"text":"the actual writes."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fix by declaring vaddr as 'u32 *' in both functions and changing"},{"depth":1,"text":"memset_vaddr in struct at_desc from 'int *' to 'u32 *'. This matches"},{"depth":1,"text":"the actual usage and eliminates the need for the (u32 *) cast."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: 5d8c5bea0da9 (\"dmaengine: at_hdmac: add COMPILE_TEST support\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Reported-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/oe-kbuild-all/202607231110.8MqNRj0Q-lkp@intel.com/"},{"depth":1,"text":"Assisted-by: opencode:big-pickle"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"}],"lineCount":19,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Reviewed-by: Frank Li <Frank.Li@nxp.com>"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" v2: remove extra cast"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/dma/at_hdmac.c | 16 ++++++++--------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/dma/at_hdmac.c b/drivers/dma/at_hdmac.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 7b6aa9bbc3c8..f24e64219fb5 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/dma/at_hdmac.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/dma/at_hdmac.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -244,7 +244,7 @@ struct at_desc {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t/* Memset temporary buffer */"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tbool\t\t\t\tmemset_buffer;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tdma_addr_t\t\t\tmemset_paddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tint\t\t\t\t*memset_vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tu32\t\t\t\t*memset_vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct atdma_sg\t\t\tsg[] __counted_by(sglen);"},{"depth":1,"text":" };"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1097,7 +1097,7 @@ atc_prep_dma_memset(struct dma_chan *chan, dma_addr_t dest, int value,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct at_dma_chan\t*atchan = to_at_dma_chan(chan);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct at_dma\t\t*atdma = to_at_dma(chan->device);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct at_desc\t\t*desc;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tvoid __iomem\t\t*vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tu32\t\t\t*vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tdma_addr_t\t\tpaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tchar\t\t\tfill_pattern;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint\t\t\tret;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1126,10 +1126,10 @@ atc_prep_dma_memset(struct dma_chan *chan, dma_addr_t dest, int value,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t/* Only the first byte of value is to be used according to dmaengine */"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tfill_pattern = (char)value;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t*(u32*)vaddr = (fill_pattern << 24) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t       (fill_pattern << 16) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t       (fill_pattern << 8) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t       fill_pattern;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t*vaddr = (fill_pattern << 24) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t (fill_pattern << 16) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t (fill_pattern << 8) |"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t  fill_pattern;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" \tdesc = kzalloc_flex(*desc, sg, 1, GFP_ATOMIC);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (!desc)"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1168,7 +1168,7 @@ atc_prep_dma_memset_sg(struct dma_chan *chan,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct at_dma\t\t*atdma = to_at_dma(chan->device);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct at_desc\t\t*desc;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tstruct scatterlist\t*sg;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tvoid __iomem\t\t*vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tu32\t\t\t*vaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tdma_addr_t\t\tpaddr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tsize_t\t\t\ttotal_len = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint\t\t\ti;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1189,7 +1189,7 @@ atc_prep_dma_memset_sg(struct dma_chan *chan,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t__func__);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\treturn NULL;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t*(u32*)vaddr = value;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t*vaddr = value;"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" \tdesc = kzalloc_flex(*desc, sg, sg_len, GFP_ATOMIC);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (!desc)"},{"depth":1,"text":"--"},{"depth":1,"tex